Third-Party Licenses
====================

This project does **not** vendor or redistribute third-party source code. It is
a set of Python packages that:

  1. depend on third-party libraries installed separately from PyPI (declared in
     each package's `pyproject.toml`), each governed by its own license; and
  2. reference external Model Context Protocol (MCP) servers that run as
     separate processes (and are documented as optional companions), and are
     not redistributed here.

This document attributes those third parties. License identifiers below are
provided for convenience; the authoritative license text ships with each
project's own distribution. No copyleft (e.g. GPL/LGPL) runtime dependency is
included.

